>> 30      1.219512195
>> 31      1.234567901
>> 32      1.25
>> 33      1.265822785
>> [...]
>
> Your math sure makes the formula you found look
> broken, not just in this case but in every case.

Probabilities above 1 are equivalent to 1; nothing too broken about
that. (The mention of integer arithmetic is a red herring, since the
_game_ isn't doing any division; it's just that an X in Y chance is
expressed as X/Y in standard notation.)

> Where did you find that formula?

mon1-343.txt, I expect. (Or someone quoting it.)

> Source divers, is that representative of what
> the game actually does?

Yep. From resist() in zap.c:

        resisted = rn2(100 + alev - dlev) < mtmp->data->mr;

where alev and dlev are the attack level of the effect and the defence
level of the monster, respectively.

